# Fact registry — {{TITLE}}

Every number and every claim that appears on a slide lives in exactly one row
here. Slides cite the ID; they never restate the value. Update the row and
nothing downstream can go stale.

**ID policy.** `F-001` upward, assigned sequentially, **stable and never
reused**. A row that turns out to be a duplicate is annotated in place
("dropped as duplicate of F-014; ID retired") rather than deleted, so an old
citation can still be resolved.

**Single home.** A value lives in one canonical row. Two exceptions, both
explicit: a source-faithful row quoting the same value from a different
document must name the canonical row in its flags; narrative pages may restate
a value for readability but must carry the ID beside it. On any conflict, this
table wins.

**Precedence.** Where sources disagree, the more accountable one wins: an
audited filing beats a press release beats a prior deck beats a conversation.
Record the disagreement with a `CONFLICT` flag and write the reasoning into
`sensitive.md` rather than quietly picking one.

## Flags

| Flag | Meaning | May it ship? |
|---|---|---|
| (none) | sourced and verified against the cited document | yes |
| `VERBAL` | told to us in conversation, not in any document | only with the flag surfaced on the face |
| `DECK-ONLY` | appears in a prior deck, unverified elsewhere | only reframed or labelled |
| `press-grade` | press or PR sourced, not company-verified | only with attribution on the face |
| `CONFLICT` | sources disagree; see sensitive.md | only after the conflict is resolved |
| `PARTIAL` | true for a subset, not the whole | only with the scope stated |
| `projection` | a forward-looking estimate | only labelled as a target or estimate |
| `unsourced` | no source found | never |

